                        "form": "Ked"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "93a851a3-a7b9-379a-a0c2-472596678a01",
                        "entry_id": "dc1a5a5b-c593-3a22-b1bf-0a456bfd5432",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Plimsolls (canvas shoes with rubber soles) of the American brand Keds."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "plural-normally"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4ef4ece9-c91e-4d51-8c50-7b7c81f425d8",
                                "sense_id": "93a851a3-a7b9-379a-a0c2-472596678a01",
                                "text": "Now for any mid-century boy worth his Keds, mastery of the pea-shooter was a skill on a par with tree fort construction, delivering a satisfactory nuggy, and frying ants with sunshine and a magnifying glass."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7ef4582b-3c50-4b60-acaa-a81e0903f179",
                                "sense_id": "93a851a3-a7b9-379a-a0c2-472596678a01",
                                "text": "Once far from the flooding light, Caleb pulled up short, and her Keds skidded out from under her on the damp pavement."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "723eccc5-af3b-464c-b5fb-118c3f38cf0a",
                                "sense_id": "93a851a3-a7b9-379a-a0c2-472596678a01",
                                "text": "As I prepared myself by putting my Keds back on (I still take my shoes off at any opportunity), my mom mumbled something under her breath at my dad."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
